{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/907046-wwycd-werewolf-edition-night-of-the-living-dead","id":907046,"title":"WWYCD (Werewolf Edition): Night of the Living Dead","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-04T03:07:45-07:00","id":907046,"title":"WWYCD (Werewolf Edition): Night of the Living Dead","content":"The original <i>Night of the Living Dead </i>was on TV and it inspired this thought exercise (which I already posted in the Mage forum). I'll copy it here and in the Vampire forum, at least, and let's get an idea for what your characters would do!<br /> <br /> Let's pose a Chronicles of Darkness version of the <i>Night of the Living Dead </i>scenario. The dead have begun to rise in a small town or city. It starts small, maybe even a local rundown graveyard or a cadaver suddenly awakening in a hospital. Maybe a patient dying in the hospital of a mysterious and rather gruesome illness. Reports of violent crimes across the county. Even cannibalism. Some force sporadically disrupts communications. Maybe similar reports come in from across the region, or even further out. Maybe you can't see that far, or don't have the luxury. Spirits speak of dangerous things lurking out in the night, more so than usual.<br /> <br /> The undead rise within minutes of anyone's death. They are tireless, mindlessly hungry, brutally strong. Some are fast, some are slow. Only destroying the brain or burning the body stops them. They can't be reasoned with, though they seem to have some ability to detect the living and travel in groups. A bite or scratch can transmit an almost universally-fatal wasting illness, although magic can cure it in those still living. The origin is unknown. Is this a terrible plague created by an <i>idigam</i>? Some death god risen from cthonian depths? A Maeljin using the bones of Father Wolf to raise up a kingdom of the dead? No one knows. The Shadow is a nightmarish realm of horrific Essence and ravenous spirits. These zombies aren't all just corpses Claimed by death-spirits, though a few of those probably appear (compounding the problem, though indistinguishable from other zombies to mortals). Spirits of death, pain, darkness, blood, and diseaes sweep through the <i>Hisil</i>. Desperation leads to <i>magath </i>that are themselves almost zombie-like, as spirits consume death-resonance to survive and become tainted by it. The mortal realm is no better, with ghosts stirred to wrath and madness, and new ghosts born every day, though many werewolves have greater concerns.<br /> <br /> What would your character do? How does he or she survive? How do your natural abilities aid you? What do you hunt, what do you try to protect? Humans? How can you hide your nature in such a desperate time, and if you can't, what does it mean? You can use some examples of common scenarios: finding a place to hole up, aiding (or preying upon) other survivors, fighting zombies, going on food runs. You can even add in zombie animals if you like (I certainly like to use 'em!). For a twist, you could even say that werewolf zombies appear, only capable of shifting between human zombie form and undead lupine forms (even Gauru?). They have a cunning, predatory intelligence, but they're still undead and malevolent. What is your plan? Do you try to escape, make a safehold, set yourself up as a would-be warlord in this chaos? Do you use the opportunity to pursue fetishes, drain or protect Loci, seek out spirits to aid you in surviving? Do you try to explore the cause of the undead rising? Or is simply surviving it enough?<br /> <br /> When there is no more room in Hell, the dead will walk the Earth. Theirs is an endless hunt, but you are no base prey. You are the mightiest hunters! If anyone can survive a Night of the Living Dead, it's you. The wolf must hunt, but how does the wolf hunt when the world falls prey to a plague of flesh-eating undead?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T07:43:14-07:00","id":907097,"title":"","content":"One of the first steps seems to be rallying the appropriate spirits, the ones who need human society running as usual to produce Resonance. Allies in the Flame court would also be very valuable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T17:52:25-07:00","id":907346,"title":"","content":"So many books about this.<br /> <br /> This is probably more my speed, compared to the mage one. Without even having to consult one another we'd probably gather up our pack and fortify an area. Our most 'alpha' wolf-blooded is wealthy and has a lot of properties we could use, but there's also islands and malls and all really seem like good places. Then we'd go out on hunts to clear out zombies and secure the areas we didn't originally choose, just in case we need a fall-back. Some of the other pack members would probably want us to take in survivors but my character would be against it, for the most part. So we'd settle that when it came up. <br /> <br /> Werewolf senses could probably scent out a zombie a mile away, and bites and blood just as easy, so there would be no, 'It's not a bite! I just cut myself on the fence!' Werewolves, at least the Uratha, are <i>way</i> capable of dealing with zombie swarms. I'd feel bad for those with the Other triggers, though, as death raging then passing out in human form is not something you would want to happen. As is common in zombie media, they're just the plot device that makes way for other antagonists, usually other humans. Unfortunately in this situation every traditional werewolf prey is suddenly given an opportunity.<br /> <br /> It would probably be easier to deal with zombies in the gurihal first, before risking the Hisil, spirits bursting at the seams with newfound power would make it deadly until the original chaos settled down. Our pack's situation is sort of odd and the chaos and destruction wrought by a zombie outbreak would probably help us more than hurt us, providing we could get everyone to safety. Most of our hated enemies are hiding behind bureaucracy and legions of meat shields, and an outbreak would severely hamper their ability to keep hiding like that, as people scattered and they couldn't fall back on the Masquerade or numbers to protect them.<br /> <br /> We don't have anyone with the fire Influence ability yet, but my guy is the least of the combatants and while he wouldn't be able to consistently make head shots he could probably go the old fashioned 'total body dismemberment' method. I just grabbed Marrow Eater after our last hunt, and it would be nice to be full up without drawing stares. It would be cool to go out 'under cover' with Cold Embrace, but I'd regret putting off the Warding gifts for so long, they seem like they would be perfect. While I like the idea that there might be werewolf zombies, I don't think it should be spread via infection, and more a result of death spirits and other things claiming dead or once-living werewolves. The idea of setting yourself up as a warlord seems a fine one, I guess it would depend on if the scenario would end or zombies are going to be a fact of life from now on.<br /> <br /> A couple questions. <b>First</b>, you said they have some ability to detect the living, do they have any interest in animals? It seems like they wouldn't but if so, the hosts would have an easier time overrunning things, and there's always the cockroach-eating scene from the original, and books like Keene's The Rising that have animals involved. <b>Second</b>, would the Nature Gift Facet Black Earth, Red Hunger work against them? It says, 'Any dead bodies within the area when this Facet is used are utterly consumed by plants, moss, and fungus, leaving not even bones behind.' Zombies seem like they would count as dead bodies, but then again vampires might too and I wouldn't make them susceptible to it.<br /> <br /> Providing the hosts didn't take over this really seems like a Pure victory scenario as spirits glut themselves and civilization is brought back a few levels. It would be very interesting to see the lodges and possibly even tribes that resulted from this. Maybe the Beshilu would recreate their Plague King.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T21:01:01-07:00","id":907432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/907046-wwycd-werewolf-edition-night-of-the-living-dead?p=907346#post907346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A couple questions. <b>First</b>, you said they have some ability to detect the living, do they have any interest in animals? It seems like they wouldn't but if so, the hosts would have an easier time overrunning things, and there's always the cockroach-eating scene from the original, and books like Keene's The Rising that have animals involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. All living things save maybe for trees are on the menu.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/907046-wwycd-werewolf-edition-night-of-the-living-dead?p=907346#post907346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Second</b>, would the Nature Gift Facet Black Earth, Red Hunger work against them? It says, 'Any dead bodies within the area when this Facet is used are utterly consumed by plants, moss, and fungus, leaving not even bones behind.' Zombies seem like they would count as dead bodies, but then again vampires might too and I wouldn't make them susceptible to it.<br /> <br /> Providing the hosts didn't take over this really seems like a Pure victory scenario as spirits glut themselves and civilization is brought back a few levels. It would be very interesting to see the lodges and possibly even tribes that resulted from this. Maybe the Beshilu would recreate their Plague King.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would have said &quot;Yes&quot; at first, but if you wouldn't let it work on vampires, I'm not sure I'd let it work on zombies. Though zombies are considerably more decayed, whatever their origin in this case, so maybe it would work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}